      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " A future represents an asynchronous computation, commonly obtained by use of",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            127,
            207
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`async`].",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            208,
            222
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            223,
            226
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " A future is a value that might not have finished computing yet. This kind of",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            227,
            307
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " \"asynchronous value\" makes it possible for a thread to continue doing useful",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            308,
            388
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " work while it waits for the value to become available.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            389,
            447
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            448,
            451
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # The `poll` method",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            452,
            475
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            476,
            479
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The core method of future, `poll`, *attempts* to resolve the future into a",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            480,
            558
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " final value. This method does not block if the value is not ready. Instead,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            559,
            638
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " the current task is scheduled to be woken up when it's possible to make",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            639,
            714
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " further progress by `poll`ing again. The `context` passed to the `poll`",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            715,
            790
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " method can provide a [`Waker`], which is a handle for waking up the current",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            791,
            870
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " task.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            871,
            880
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            881,
            884
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " When using a future, you generally won't call `poll` directly, but instead",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            885,
            963
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `.await` the value.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            964,
            987
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            988,
            991
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`async`]: ../../std/keyword.async.html",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            992,
            1035
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`Waker`]: crate::task::Waker",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1036,
            1069
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1070,
            1091
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1092,
            1112
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": null,
          "path": "must_use",
          "range": [
            1113,
