    {
      "ancestors": [
        0
      ],
      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " Attempts to resolve the future to a final value, registering",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1553,
            1617
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " the current task for wakeup if the value is not yet available.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1622,
            1688
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1693,
            1696
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # Return value",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1701,
            1719
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1724,
            1727
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This function returns:",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1732,
            1758
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1763,
            1766
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " - [`Poll::Pending`] if the future is not ready yet",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1771,
            1825
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " - [`Poll::Ready(val)`] with the result `val` of this future if it",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1830,
            1899
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "   finished successfully.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1904,
            1932
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1937,
            1940
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Once a future has finished, clients should not `poll` it again.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1945,
            2012
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2017,
            2020
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " When a future is not ready yet, `poll` returns `Poll::Pending` and",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2025,
            2095
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " stores a clone of the [`Waker`] copied from the current [`Context`].",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2100,
            2172
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " This [`Waker`] is then woken once the future can make progress.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2177,
            2244
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " For example, a future waiting for a socket to become",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2249,
            2305
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " readable would call `.clone()` on the [`Waker`] and store it.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2310,
            2375
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " When a signal arrives elsewhere indicating that the socket is readable,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2380,
            2455
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`Waker::wake`] is called and the socket future's task is awoken.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2460,
            2529
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Once a task has been woken up, it should attempt to `poll` the future",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2534,
            2607
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " again, which may or may not produce a final value.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2612,
            2666
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2671,
            2674
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Note that on multiple calls to `poll`, only the [`Waker`] from the",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2679,
            2749
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " [`Context`] passed to the most recent call should be scheduled to",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2754,
            2823
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " receive a wakeup.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2828,
            2849
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2854,
            2857
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # Runtime characteristics",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2862,
            2891
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2896,
            2899
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Futures alone are *inert*; they must be *actively* `poll`ed for the",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2904,
            2975
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " underlying computation to make progress, meaning that each time the",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            2980,
            3051
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " current task is woken up, it should actively re-`poll` pending futures",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3056,
            3130
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " that it still has an interest in.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3135,
            3172
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3177,
            3180
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Having said that, some Futures may represent a value that is being",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3185,
            3255
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " computed in a different task. In this case, the future's underlying",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3260,
            3331
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " computation is simply acting as a conduit for a value being computed",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3336,
            3408
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " by that other task, which will proceed independently of the Future.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3413,
            3484
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Futures of this kind are typically obtained when spawning a new task into an",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3489,
            3569
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " async runtime.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3574,
            3592
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3597,
            3600
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The `poll` function should not be called repeatedly in a tight loop --",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3605,
            3679
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " instead, it should only be called when the future indicates that it is",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3684,
            3758
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ready to make progress (by calling `wake()`). If you're familiar with the",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3763,
            3840
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `poll(2)` or `select(2)` syscalls on Unix it's worth noting that futures",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3845,
            3921
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " typically do *not* suffer the same problems of \"all wakeups must poll",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            3926,
            3999
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " all events\"; they are more like `epoll(4)`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4004,
            4051
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4056,
            4059
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " An implementation of `poll` should strive to return quickly, and should",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4064,
            4139
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " not block. Returning quickly prevents unnecessarily clogging up",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4144,
            4211
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " threads or event loops. If it is known ahead of time that a call to",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4216,
            4287
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `poll` may end up taking a while, the work should be offloaded to a",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4292,
            4363
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " thread pool (or something similar) to ensure that `poll` can return",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4368,
            4439
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " quickly.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4444,
            4456
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4461,
            4464
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # Panics",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4469,
            4481
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4486,
            4489
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Once a future has completed (returned `Ready` from `poll`), calling its",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4494,
            4569
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `poll` method again may panic, block forever, or cause other kinds of",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4574,
            4647
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " problems; the `Future` trait places no requirements on the effects of",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4652,
            4725
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " such a call. However, as the `poll` method is not marked `unsafe`,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4730,
            4800
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Rust's usual rules apply: calls must never cause undefined behavior",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4805,
            4876
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " (memory corruption, incorrect use of `unsafe` functions, or the like),",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            4881,
            4955
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " regardless of the future's state.",
          "path": "doc",
